<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mongol conquest of the Song dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1235">1235</a>–<a href="/years/1279">1279</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Mongol campaigns against the Song</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mongol conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> was a long series of campaigns from 1235 to 1279. Song resistance was strong, with river defences and fortified cities such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiangyang">Xiangyang</a> holding out for years. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> finally completed the conquest in 1279, uniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongol-conquest-of-the-song-dynasty.jpg" alt="Mongol conquest of the Song dynasty" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SS · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mongol_Song_Wars.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
